      "side": 1,
      "message": "In a follow up (in parallel of the rest) can we try to make a utility so we can write something like:\n\n```\nfor (auto [offset, size] : IterateBitRanges(dirty)) {\n   pipelineOffset \u003d ... (offset)\n   // CmdPushConstants pipelineOffset, size\n}\n```\n\nIt should be possible to make each iteration constant time with bit twiddling.\n\n```\nif (empty) { return end() }\nshift \u003d ScanForward(mMask)\nmOffset +\u003d shift\nmMask \u003e\u003e\u003d shift\nsubMask \u003d mask \u0026 ~(mask + 1)\nmMask \u0026\u003d !subMask\nreturn {mOffset, subMask.count()}\n```\n\nNot sure if it is faster in practice than a loop.",
